From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:08:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Cleanup that needs no decision (U06)

Archive hazard: delete client/src/data/*-articles*.ts (20 files) and
devotionals.ts, devotionals-2.ts. Nothing imports them (grep, then pnpm
check); they carried unconfirmed first-person scenes as James.
client/src/data/articles/ stays (server/routers.ts imports it).

Stale tool copy: the nine /tools registry descriptions that named retired
sections ("Part of Integrated Life", "Part of the Theological Depth
section", "the pillar built to dismantle the lens") now say what each tool
does. Which Lens Has You? no longer ends in "Enter the pillar": each lens
points straight at a live place (a shelf section, a tool, or church
history), with an optional second door that, when it is an essay, shows
only while that essay is on the shelf. The runner-up line links its lens's
reading directly.

Folds, one permanent hop each, with redirectTo stubs in App.tsx:
/grief, /faith-crisis, /marriage-crisis, /parenting-help, /deconstruction
and /church-hurt to their Find Help pages; /parenting and /for-families to
/family; /marriage to /help/marriage. The two old essay URLs that landed
on /parenting now land on /life/the-wayward-child in one hop. The page
files stay in the repo.

Every live link to a folded page is re-pointed: the Start Here diagnostic
and quiz, /family's cards, /life, the deconstruction FAQ panel, ten
Integrated Life connections, two Wisdom topics (index rebuilt), and the
Find Help kits (two self-links after the fold are dropped). The sitemap,
prerendered heads, and the API's fallback sitemap no longer list them.

Pathway subtitles no longer promise essays that are off the site; each
names what the page shows today (index rebuilt).

site-structure.test.ts holds the nine new folds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
