-
-<p>The church must do five things, and it must do them now, without further delay or qualification.</p>
-
-<p>First, it must name abuse from the pulpit. Not once. Regularly. The congregation must hear, from their pastor, in the context of worship, that abuse is sin — that it is not headship, not discipline, not a marital problem. It is sin. And the church does not tolerate it.</p>
