-
-<p>One of the most insidious patterns in marriages with children is the displacement of marital energy onto the children. The parents stop investing in each other and invest entirely in the children — their activities, their education, their emotional development, their social lives. The children become the project, and the marriage becomes the infrastructure that supports the project. The couple does not think of themselves as a couple. They think of themselves as co-managers of a small enterprise, and the enterprise's product is well-adjusted children.</p>
