-
-<p>It looks like conversations about something other than the children. This is harder than it sounds, because the children provide a safe, shared topic that requires no vulnerability. Talking about the kids is easy. Talking about your inner life, your fears, your desires, your disappointments — that is hard. And hard is exactly what the marriage needs, because the marriage was built on two people knowing each other, and you cannot know someone who only talks about logistics.</p>
-
-<p>It looks like the decision — made deliberately and counter-culturally — to say no to the children's demands in order to say yes to the marriage. Not always. Not cruelly. But sometimes, the family does not attend the tournament because the parents need a weekend together. Sometimes the children go to bed early because the adults need an evening. Sometimes the answer to "Can I have" is "Not tonight, because Mom and Dad need time." The children will survive the disappointment. The marriage may not survive the neglect.</p>
