-<p>Almost every Christian parent I know carries guilt about family devotions. They are sure they should be doing them, sure they are doing them wrong or not enough, sure that other families have some serene candlelit thing they cannot achieve. The guilt is enormous and it is nearly universal and it produces two outcomes, both bad. Either the parents give up entirely and carry the guilt, or they grind out a joyless ritual and call it obedience while their kids quietly conclude that faith is a chore.</p>
