-
-<p>But Graham's significance extended far beyond his preaching. In 1956, he founded <em>Christianity Today</em>, a magazine intended to be the evangelical alternative to the liberal <em>Christian Century</em>. Henry served as its first editor. The magazine was explicitly designed to demonstrate that evangelical Christianity could be intellectually rigorous, culturally engaged, and theologically grounded. For a generation, it largely succeeded.</p>
-
