-<h2>What Christendom Was</h2>
-
-<p>Christendom is not a synonym for Christianity. Christianity is a faith, a set of convictions about who God is and what God has done. Christendom is a political and cultural arrangement in which that faith becomes the organizing principle of an entire civilization, fused with state power, embedded in law, assumed in education, and enforced, where necessary, by coercion.</p>
