-<p>These are not merely statistical declines. They represent the end of a civilizational paradigm. For centuries, European culture was Christian culture. Its art was Christian art, its architecture was Christian architecture, its moral vocabulary was Christian moral vocabulary. When Dante wrote the <em>Divine Comedy</em>, he assumed that every reader shared his cosmology. When Bach composed the <em>Mass in B Minor</em>, he assumed that every listener knew what a mass was. Those assumptions no longer hold. European civilization has not replaced Christianity with an alternative comprehensive worldview. It has simply moved into a condition that Taylor calls "exclusive humanism," a vision of human flourishing that makes no reference to anything beyond the immanent world.</p>
