-<p>The digital revolution accelerated this trend. A generation raised on the internet — accustomed to customization, skeptical of institutional gatekeepers, fluent in the language of brands and experiences — found the non-denominational model intuitive in a way that denominational structures were not. The non-denominational church's emphasis on personal experience over institutional identity, on accessible communication over traditional vocabulary, and on contemporary relevance over historical continuity mapped naturally onto the assumptions of digital culture.</p>
