-
-<p>The claim to be "non-denominational" is, at its core, a claim to have no theological commitments beyond the Bible. But this claim does not survive even casual examination. Every non-denominational church makes theological decisions — about baptism, about the Lord's Supper, about the role of women, about soteriology, about eschatology, about the gifts of the Spirit — and those decisions place it within identifiable theological traditions, whether it acknowledges this or not.</p>
-
