-
-<p>None of this is necessarily wrong. But it is a tradition. The worship songs of Chris Tomlin and Elevation Worship are no less culturally situated than the hymns of Isaac Watts or Charles Wesley. The topical sermon series is no less a homiletical choice than the liturgical lectionary. The decision to practice believer's baptism by immersion is no less a theological commitment than the decision to baptize infants. The difference is that denominational churches typically know where their practices come from and why, while non-denominational churches often treat their practices as simply "what the Bible says" — unaware that they are operating within a tradition that has a history, influences, and assumptions.</p>
