-
-<p>Many churches have attempted to resolve the tension through "blended worship" — services that combine elements of both traditions. A typical blended service might include a call to worship and a responsive reading (liturgical elements), followed by a set of contemporary worship songs, a topical sermon, and a closing hymn. Some churches offer separate services in different styles; others attempt to weave the traditions together in a single service.</p>
