-<h2>Why Young People Are Returning to Liturgy</h2>
-
-<p>One of the more striking trends in American Christianity over the past decade has been the movement of young adults — particularly those raised in contemporary evangelical churches — toward liturgical traditions: Anglicanism, Catholicism, Orthodoxy, and liturgical expressions of Lutheranism and Presbyterianism. The trend is not statistically enormous, but it is culturally significant, and it has generated a substantial body of personal testimony and sociological analysis.</p>
