-
-<p>The most productive way to evaluate any worship practice is to ask not "Do I like it?" but "What is it doing to me?" Worship is not entertainment. It is not self-expression. It is, in the deepest sense, <em>formation</em> — the slow, repetitive, often unconscious process by which a community is shaped into a particular kind of people. The question is not whether the music is good or the sermon is interesting. The question is: Over a lifetime of participation, what kind of Christian will this worship produce?</p>
