-<p>The answer, which the early church learned at extraordinary cost, is that the Bible does not interpret itself. Every heresy in the history of Christianity has claimed biblical support. Arius quoted Scripture to prove that Christ was a creature. The Gnostics quoted Scripture to prove that the material world was evil. The Docetists quoted Scripture to prove that Christ did not really suffer. The creeds were not additions to Scripture. They were the church's authoritative summary of what Scripture teaches — drawn up because false teachers were using Scripture to teach things that Scripture, rightly understood, does not say.</p>
