-
-<p>The reasons people give for leaving the church are remarkably consistent across studies. The Public Religion Research Institute's 2023 survey of religiously unaffiliated Americans found the same cluster of reasons near the top of the list: negative treatment of LGBTQ+ people, clergy sexual abuse scandals, the church's association with partisan politics, and a general sense that religious people are judgmental or hypocritical (36 percent). These are not vague spiritual dissatisfactions. They are specific, concrete grievances about institutional behavior.</p>
