-
-<p>The sexual abuse crisis — spanning Catholic, Protestant, and independent churches — has done incalculable damage to the church's moral authority. The Catholic Church's abuse scandal, exposed in devastating detail by the <em>Boston Globe</em>'s Spotlight team in 2002 and subsequently documented in dioceses around the world, revealed not merely the existence of predatory priests but a systematic institutional effort to conceal their crimes, protect the perpetrators, and silence the victims.</p>
-
