-<p>The abuse crisis is not merely a scandal. It is an indictment of institutional structures that prioritize the institution's reputation over the safety of the people it claims to serve. And for many who have left, it is the single most powerful evidence that the institution has lost its moral bearing. A church that cannot protect children has forfeited its claim to moral authority on any other subject.</p>
