-
-<p>Here is the distinction that most church leaders fail to grasp, or perhaps refuse to grasp because it is too threatening to their institutional interests: the majority of people who leave the church are not leaving God. They are leaving the institution. And these are not the same thing.</p>
-
-<p>The Pew Research Center has consistently found that among the religiously unaffiliated, a significant majority retain some form of spiritual belief. Many believe in God or a higher power. Many pray. Many describe themselves as "spiritual but not religious" — a phrase that institutional Christians tend to mock but that deserves to be taken seriously as a description of a genuine spiritual posture. These are people who have concluded that the institutional church is not the best vehicle for their spiritual life. Given the institutional church's track record, this is not an unreasonable conclusion.</p>
