-<p>This assumption is wrong. It is wrong historically, wrong theologically, and wrong pastorally. And the church's panicked response to deconstruction is itself a significant cause of the very departures it claims to lament. When a tradition tells its members that honest questioning is the first step toward apostasy, it creates a binary that forces people out: either accept everything without examination, or leave entirely. Many are choosing to leave — not because deconstruction destroyed their faith, but because the church refused to make room for it.</p>
