-    body: `<p>The standard narrative goes something like this: In 1973, the Supreme Court handed down <em>Roe v. Wade</em>, and evangelical Christians, roused by the slaughter of the unborn, organized politically to defend the sanctity of life. Out of this moral conviction, the Religious Right was born — a grassroots movement of people of faith who reluctantly entered the political arena because the stakes were too high for silence.</p>
