-<p>Paul Weyrich, the conservative political operative who co-founded the Heritage Foundation and who would later co-found the Moral Majority with Jerry Falwell, was explicit about this. In remarks at a 1990 conference, recounted by the historian Randall Balmer, Weyrich stated: "What galvanized the Christian community was not abortion, school prayer, or the ERA. I am living witness to that because I was trying to get those people interested in those issues and I utterly failed. What changed their mind was Jimmy Carter's intervention against the Christian schools, trying to deny them tax-exempt status on the basis of so-called de facto segregation."</p>
