-
-<p>The most devastating consequence of the church's political alignment has been the loss of its prophetic voice. The prophetic tradition in Scripture is characterized by a willingness to speak truth to power regardless of political consequence — to challenge kings, to confront empires, to name injustice wherever it is found, including and especially within the community of faith itself. The prophet stands outside the structures of power and speaks into them. The prophet is beholden to God, not to any political faction.</p>
