-<p>The prophetic tradition has always been costly. Prophets are not popular. They are not invited to the White House. They do not receive standing ovations at political conventions. They speak truth that power does not want to hear, and they pay the price for it. The question before the American church is whether it wants to be prophetic or powerful — because the history of the past fifty years demonstrates, with painful clarity, that it cannot be both.</p>`,
