-
-<p>Can you trust the Bible? Not if you mean: can you treat it as a science textbook, a history textbook, or a systematic theology that dropped complete from heaven? No. But if you mean: can you trust it as the primary witness to God's self-revelation, as a text that has been tested by centuries of critical scrutiny and has survived, as the book that still has the power to name what is wrong with the world and point toward what would make it right — then yes. You can trust it. Not because it is simple, but because it is honest. And honest things are worth trusting, even when — especially when — they do not give us everything we wish they would.</p>`,
