-<p>Annihilationism, also known as conditional immortality, holds that the unsaved do not suffer eternally but are ultimately destroyed — that the final punishment is not everlasting torment but the cessation of existence. On this view, immortality is not an inherent property of the human soul but a gift of God, granted to the redeemed and withheld from the lost. The wicked are raised, judged, punished proportionally to their sins, and then annihilated. They cease to exist.</p>
