-<p>The third casualty was the next generation. Millennials and Generation Z were raised in the culture war. They watched it from the inside. And what they saw — the selective outrage, the political captivity, the gap between proclaimed values and institutional behavior — drove them away in historically unprecedented numbers. The Barna Group's research has consistently shown that young adults associate Christianity with being anti-gay, judgmental, hypocritical, and overly political. These are not misperceptions imposed from outside. They are observations drawn from direct experience of the culture war church.</p>
