-
-<p>I find myself persuaded that the restrictive texts are more situationally bound than the tradition I was raised in allowed, and that the sweep of Scripture, the prophetesses, the apostle Junia, the deacon Phoebe, the reversal Christ works on the curse, leans toward a fuller participation of women than most of my churches practiced. That is where I land, and it comes from the broadly egalitarian tradition, though I hold it without contempt for the other side.</p>
